  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tSelf Assessment \n\t\tSelf Assessment Help Guide\n\n### How to transfer partnership directors details from the SA800 to the SA100\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 16 Aug, 2021 at  1:51 PM\n\n\t\tNavigation: Self Assessment > SA100 > +SA100 > Supplementary form > Partnership\n\n Please click here to watch a video on how to link your SA800 and SA100 for partnerships           \n\nHelp/Guide: \n\nNew update 12/08/21! You can now transfer over the Partnership details from the SA800 to the SA100 automatically\n\nPlease head to you SA100 return Click here to find out how to create an SA100\n\nClick on + Supplementary form and select Partnership or Partnership Short then click the 'X' button\n\nScroll to find the section in the Supplementary Pages Tab and click on a link to start filling out the information\n\nClick on the dropdown box on the right hand side\nSelect the partnership return\nClick link SA800 return\n\nThe information will fill out automatically\n\nPlease then click save\n\nHaving Issues?-Let's troubleshoot common issues\n\nDoes the partner in the sa800 (under SA800 > settings> Partners) have the same UTR as the Individual?\nIn the SA800 form are all of the Partners' shares and income allocated?\nIn the SA100 have you selected the correct partnership form  from the drop down before clicking link SA800?\nIf you have added any supplementary pages in SA800 you should select Partnership, if you have added no supplementary pages you should choose partnership short\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
